%%DOC welcome
path.en: LeonOS/Welcome
path.zh: LeonOS/欢迎
title.en: Welcome
title.zh: 欢迎
author: LeonOS Team
version: 1.0
%%LANG en
# Welcome to LeonOS Help

LeonOS Help stores several Markdown pages inside one `.hlp` file. Use the tree on the left to choose a page, then read the document on the right.

## Navigation

- Use **Back** and **Forward** to jump between pages you have visited.
- Use the language selector to switch this help window between English and Chinese.
- Use the mouse wheel to scroll long documents.

## Included topics

| Topic | Purpose |
| File permissions | Explains R, W, X, Delete and Manage |
| Blue screen errors | Explains STOP reasons, CPU vectors and Page Fault flags |
| Help file format | Shows how developers can write `.hlp` files |

%%LANG zh
# 欢迎使用 LeonOS 帮助

LeonOS 帮助把多个 Markdown 页面放在同一个 `.hlp` 文件里。左边选择文档，右边阅读正文。

## 导航

- 使用 **后退** 和 **前进** 在访问过的页面之间跳转。
- 使用语言选择器在当前帮助窗口内切换 English / 中文。
- 使用鼠标滚轮滚动长文档。

## 已包含主题

| 主题 | 说明 |
| 文件权限 | 解释 R、W、X、Delete、Manage |
| 蓝屏错误 | 解释 STOP 原因、CPU 向量和 Page Fault 标志 |
| 帮助文件格式 | 说明开发者如何编写 `.hlp` 文件 |

%%ENDDOC

%%DOC system.bugcheck
path.en: System/Blue screen errors
path.zh: 系统/蓝屏错误
title.en: Blue screen errors
title.zh: 蓝屏错误
author: LeonOS Team
version: 1.0
%%LANG en
# Blue screen errors

LeonOS shows a blue bugcheck screen when the kernel cannot safely continue. The screen starts with a `STOP:` reason, then diagnostic fields such as `PID`, `TASK`, `MODE`, `VECTOR`, `ERROR`, `RIP`, `RSP`, `SS`, `CS`, `RFLAGS`, `CR2`, `TICKS` and `UPTIME_MS`.

## How to read the screen

| Field | Meaning |
| STOP | The primary reason. Match this first. |
| PID / TASK | The current task when the stop happened. |
| MODE | `kernel` means kernel or trusted system code; `user` means a Ring-3 context was active. |
| VECTOR | CPU exception vector number. `14` is Page Fault. |
| ERROR | CPU error code. For Page Fault, use the `PF FLAGS` line. |
| RIP / RSP | Instruction pointer and stack pointer at the fault. |
| CR2 | Faulting virtual address for Page Fault. |
| TICKS / UPTIME_MS | Time since boot, useful for matching serial logs. |

## STOP reasons

| STOP reason | Meaning | Usual next step |
| KERNEL PANIC | Kernel code called `panic()` or `bugcheck_panic()`. The detail line is the panic message. | Search the message in the source tree or serial log. |
| Unhandled Page Fault | A kernel-mode page fault, or a page fault that could not be recovered by lazy mapping. | Check `CR2`, `RIP`, and `PF FLAGS`. |
| Window Server Page Fault | The desktop/window server faulted. LeonOS stops because continuing could corrupt GUI ownership. | Check the window server task and the faulting address. |
| Divide By Zero | CPU vector 0. Code divided by zero. | Inspect the function at `RIP`. |
| Debug Exception | CPU vector 1. Debug trap. | Usually a bad debug state or unexpected trap. |
| Non Maskable Interrupt | CPU vector 2. NMI. | Treat as hardware or emulator-level interruption. |
| Breakpoint | CPU vector 3. Breakpoint instruction reached. | Remove unintended breakpoint or inspect debug path. |
| Overflow | CPU vector 4. Overflow trap. | Inspect arithmetic path near `RIP`. |
| Bound Range Exceeded | CPU vector 5. Bound check failed. | Inspect array/range code. |
| Invalid Opcode | CPU vector 6. Unknown or unsupported instruction. | Check compiler output, CPU feature use, or corrupted code. |
| Device Not Available | CPU vector 7. FPU/SIMD device state not available. | Check task/FPU setup. |
| Double Fault | CPU vector 8. The CPU faulted while handling another fault. | Often stack, IDT, TSS or severe memory corruption. |
| Invalid TSS | CPU vector 10. Task-state segment is invalid. | Check TSS/GDT setup. |
| Segment Not Present | CPU vector 11. Segment descriptor is unavailable. | Check GDT/segment selector state. |
| Stack Segment Fault | CPU vector 12. Stack segment fault. | Check stack selector and stack pointer. |
| General Protection Fault | CPU vector 13. Protection rule violation. | Check bad selectors, privilege transitions, invalid descriptors or privileged instructions. |
| Page Fault | CPU vector 14. Memory translation or protection fault. | Decode `PF FLAGS` and `CR2`. |
| x87 Floating Point Fault | CPU vector 16. x87 floating-point exception. | Check floating-point state and exception masks. |
| Alignment Check | CPU vector 17. Alignment check exception. | Check unaligned memory access under alignment checking. |
| Machine Check | CPU vector 18. CPU reported a machine check. | Treat as hardware/emulator fatal state. |
| SIMD Floating Point Fault | CPU vector 19. SSE/SIMD floating-point exception. | Check SIMD state and exception masks. |
| Virtualization Exception | CPU vector 20. Virtualization exception. | Check VM/emulator or virtualization feature use. |
| Control Protection Exception | CPU vector 21. Control-flow protection exception. | Check control protection state if enabled. |
| Hypervisor Injection Exception | CPU vector 28. Hypervisor-injected exception. | Check hypervisor/emulator state. |
| VMM Communication Exception | CPU vector 29. VMM communication exception. | Check hypervisor communication path. |
| Security Exception | CPU vector 30. CPU security exception. | Check CPU security feature state. |
| CPU Exception | Any other vector. | Use `VECTOR`, `ERROR` and `RIP` to identify the source. |

## Page Fault flags

When `VECTOR` is `14`, the blue screen shows `PF FLAGS`.

| Flag | Meaning when 1 | Meaning when 0 |
| P | Protection violation on a present page. | Page was not present. |
| W | Fault happened during a write. | Fault happened during a read. |
| U | Fault came from user mode. | Fault came from supervisor/kernel mode. |
| RSVD | Reserved page-table bit was set. | No reserved-bit violation. |
| IF | Fault happened during instruction fetch. | Fault happened during data access. |

## User application faults

Most ordinary Ring-3 application page faults do not blue-screen the system. LeonOS terminates the application, uses exit code `0x8000000e`, and posts an `Application Page Fault` report on the desktop. A user-mode page fault becomes a blue screen mainly when the current task is the window server or when no safe recovery path exists.

%%LANG zh
# 蓝屏错误

当内核无法安全继续运行时，LeonOS 会显示蓝屏 bugcheck。屏幕顶部会显示 `STOP:` 原因，后面是 `PID`、`TASK`、`MODE`、`VECTOR`、`ERROR`、`RIP`、`RSP`、`SS`、`CS`、`RFLAGS`、`CR2`、`TICKS`、`UPTIME_MS` 等诊断字段。

## 如何阅读蓝屏

| 字段 | 含义 |
| STOP | 主要停止原因，优先匹配这一项。 |
| PID / TASK | 触发停止时的当前任务。 |
| MODE | `kernel` 表示内核或受信系统代码；`user` 表示当时处在 Ring-3 上下文。 |
| VECTOR | CPU 异常向量号。`14` 表示 Page Fault。 |
| ERROR | CPU 错误码。Page Fault 时主要看 `PF FLAGS` 行。 |
| RIP / RSP | 出错时的指令指针和栈指针。 |
| CR2 | Page Fault 时的出错虚拟地址。 |
| TICKS / UPTIME_MS | 启动后的时间，方便和串口日志对应。 |

## STOP 原因

| STOP 原因 | 含义 | 通常怎么查 |
| KERNEL PANIC | 内核代码调用了 `panic()` 或 `bugcheck_panic()`。detail 行就是 panic 消息。 | 在源码或串口日志里搜索该消息。 |
| Unhandled Page Fault | 内核态页面错误，或懒加载映射无法恢复的页面错误。 | 查看 `CR2`、`RIP` 和 `PF FLAGS`。 |
| Window Server Page Fault | 桌面/窗口服务出错。LeonOS 会停止，因为继续运行可能破坏 GUI 所有权。 | 检查窗口服务任务和出错地址。 |
| Divide By Zero | CPU 向量 0，除零。 | 查看 `RIP` 附近的函数。 |
| Debug Exception | CPU 向量 1，调试异常。 | 通常是错误的调试状态或意外 trap。 |
| Non Maskable Interrupt | CPU 向量 2，不可屏蔽中断。 | 按硬件或模拟器层中断处理。 |
| Breakpoint | CPU 向量 3，执行了断点指令。 | 移除意外断点，或检查调试路径。 |
| Overflow | CPU 向量 4，溢出 trap。 | 检查 `RIP` 附近的算术逻辑。 |
| Bound Range Exceeded | CPU 向量 5，范围检查失败。 | 检查数组或范围逻辑。 |
| Invalid Opcode | CPU 向量 6，无效或不支持的指令。 | 检查编译输出、CPU 特性使用或代码损坏。 |
| Device Not Available | CPU 向量 7，FPU/SIMD 设备状态不可用。 | 检查任务和 FPU 初始化。 |
| Double Fault | CPU 向量 8，处理异常时再次异常。 | 常见原因是栈、IDT、TSS 或严重内存破坏。 |
| Invalid TSS | CPU 向量 10，TSS 无效。 | 检查 TSS/GDT 设置。 |
| Segment Not Present | CPU 向量 11，段描述符不存在。 | 检查 GDT 和段选择子状态。 |
| Stack Segment Fault | CPU 向量 12，栈段异常。 | 检查栈选择子和栈指针。 |
| General Protection Fault | CPU 向量 13，保护规则被违反。 | 检查错误选择子、特权级切换、无效描述符或特权指令。 |
| Page Fault | CPU 向量 14，内存转换或权限错误。 | 解读 `PF FLAGS` 和 `CR2`。 |
| x87 Floating Point Fault | CPU 向量 16，x87 浮点异常。 | 检查浮点状态和异常屏蔽。 |
| Alignment Check | CPU 向量 17，对齐检查异常。 | 检查开启对齐检查后的非对齐内存访问。 |
| Machine Check | CPU 向量 18，CPU 报告机器检查。 | 按硬件或模拟器致命状态处理。 |
| SIMD Floating Point Fault | CPU 向量 19，SSE/SIMD 浮点异常。 | 检查 SIMD 状态和异常屏蔽。 |
| Virtualization Exception | CPU 向量 20，虚拟化异常。 | 检查 VM/模拟器或虚拟化特性使用。 |
| Control Protection Exception | CPU 向量 21，控制流保护异常。 | 如果启用了控制保护，检查对应状态。 |
| Hypervisor Injection Exception | CPU 向量 28，Hypervisor 注入异常。 | 检查 hypervisor/模拟器状态。 |
| VMM Communication Exception | CPU 向量 29，VMM 通信异常。 | 检查 hypervisor 通信路径。 |
| Security Exception | CPU 向量 30，CPU 安全异常。 | 检查 CPU 安全特性状态。 |
| CPU Exception | 其他向量。 | 用 `VECTOR`、`ERROR` 和 `RIP` 定位来源。 |

## Page Fault 标志

当 `VECTOR` 是 `14` 时，蓝屏会显示 `PF FLAGS`。

| 标志 | 为 1 时 | 为 0 时 |
| P | 页面存在，但发生权限违规。 | 页面不存在。 |
| W | 写入时出错。 | 读取时出错。 |
| U | 来自用户态。 | 来自 supervisor/内核态。 |
| RSVD | 页表保留位被设置。 | 没有保留位违规。 |
| IF | 取指令时出错。 | 数据访问时出错。 |

## 用户程序页面错误

普通 Ring-3 应用的 Page Fault 通常不会导致系统蓝屏。LeonOS 会结束该应用，退出码为 `0x8000000e`，并在桌面弹出 `Application Page Fault` 报告。用户态页面错误主要在当前任务是窗口服务，或没有安全恢复路径时才会变成蓝屏。

%%ENDDOC

%%DOC fs.permissions
path.en: System/File permissions
path.zh: 系统/文件权限
title.en: File permissions
title.zh: 文件权限
author: LeonOS Team
version: 1.0
%%LANG en
# File permissions

LeonOS uses a Windows-style permission model for files and directories. The current v1 permission bits are stored in ACL metadata and checked by kernel file operations.

## Permission bits

| Bit | Meaning |
| R / Read | Read a file, list a directory, or view basic metadata. |
| W / Write | Create files, write existing files, or modify directory contents. |
| X / Execute | Run an `.elf` file or traverse a directory while resolving a path. |
| Delete | Remove or rename the object. |
| Manage | Change permissions, repair ACL metadata, or take ownership when allowed. |

## Important rules

- Administrators can manage system-wide objects and repair broken ACL metadata.
- Normal users are expected to control their own `/users/<name>` files.
- Opening a shortcut checks permission on both the `.lnk` file and its target.
- Missing ACL metadata falls back to system default rules.

%%LANG zh
# 文件权限

LeonOS 使用类似 Windows 的文件和文件夹权限模型。当前 v1 权限位保存在 ACL 元数据里，并由内核文件操作进行检查。

## 权限位

| 位 | 含义 |
| R / Read | 读取文件、列出目录，或查看基础属性。 |
| W / Write | 创建文件、写入已有文件，或修改目录内容。 |
| X / Execute | 运行 `.elf` 文件，或在路径解析时穿过目录。 |
| Delete | 删除或重命名对象。 |
| Manage | 修改权限、修复 ACL 元数据，或在允许时接管所有权。 |

## 重要规则

- 管理员可以管理系统对象，并修复损坏的 ACL 元数据。
- 普通用户默认管理自己的 `/users/<name>` 文件。
- 打开快捷方式时，会同时检查 `.lnk` 本身和目标文件的权限。
- 缺失 ACL 元数据时，会按系统默认规则合成权限。

%%ENDDOC

%%DOC help.format
path.en: Developers/Help file format
path.zh: 开发者/帮助文件格式
title.en: Help file format
title.zh: 帮助文件格式
author: LeonOS Team
version: 1.0
%%LANG en
# Help file format

A `.hlp` file is a plain text container. It starts with file metadata, then one or more document pages.

```text
    %%HLP
    title.en: My Help
    title.zh: 我的帮助
    author: Example
    version: 1.0

    %%DOC page.id
    path.en: Section/Page title
    path.zh: 分类/页面标题
    title.en: Page title
    title.zh: 页面标题
    author: Example
    version: 1.0
    %%LANG en
    # Markdown page
    Body text.
    %%LANG zh
    # Markdown 页面
    正文。
    %%ENDDOC
```

Document ids may contain letters, digits, `.`, `_` and `-`. The `path.en` and `path.zh` fields build the left-side tree.

%%LANG zh
# 帮助文件格式

`.hlp` 文件是纯文本容器。文件开头是文件信息，后面可以包含多个文档页面。

```text
    %%HLP
    title.en: My Help
    title.zh: 我的帮助
    author: Example
    version: 1.0

    %%DOC page.id
    path.en: Section/Page title
    path.zh: 分类/页面标题
    title.en: Page title
    title.zh: 页面标题
    author: Example
    version: 1.0
    %%LANG en
    # Markdown page
    Body text.
    %%LANG zh
    # Markdown 页面
    正文。
    %%ENDDOC
```

文档 id 可以包含字母、数字、`.`、`_`、`-`。`path.en` 和 `path.zh` 会生成左侧目录树。

%%ENDDOC
